---
import Icon from '../../components/Icon.astro';
import { execution, stages, stageCopy } from './model';
import './curation.css';
const fixtures = execution.fixtures;
const targets = fixtures.slice(0, 2);
const controls = fixtures.slice(2);
const audits = execution.requests.filter(request => request.label.includes('audit read'));
---
<section class="cl" data-curation-lab data-stage="before" aria-labelledby="cl-title">
  <div class="cl-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Recorded endpoint proof / synthetic fixtures</p><h2 id="cl-title">A small edit.<br /> <em>An inspectable trail.</em></h2></div><p>These controls replay a completed Laravel test. They are a portfolio exhibit, not shipped curator UI.</p></div>
  <div class="cl-stage-layout">
    <div class="cl-stage-controls">
      <div class="cl-stages" role="group" aria-label="Choose a recorded state">{stages.map((stage, i) => <button type="button" data-stage-button={stage} aria-pressed={i === 0} disabled><span>0{i + 1}</span> {stageCopy[stage].label}</button>)}</div>
      <div class="cl-story"><p class="cl-filter"><Icon name="corner-box" /> Exact name match · type: <strong>product</strong></p><h3 data-stage-title>{stageCopy.before.title}</h3><p data-stage-copy>{stageCopy.before.copy}</p><button class="cl-primary" type="button" data-next disabled><span>{stageCopy.before.action}</span><Icon name="arrow-right" /></button><p class="cl-status" role="status" aria-live="polite" data-stage-status>{stageCopy.before.status}</p></div>
      <div class="cl-checks" aria-label="Verified result"><p><strong>2</strong><span>identity fields changed</span></p><p><strong>4</strong><span>source links retained</span></p><p><strong>2</strong><span>full control rows unchanged</span></p></div>
      <a class="cl-audit-jump" href="#cl-audit-title" data-open-audits>Read the forward and inverse audits <Icon name="arrow-down" /></a>
    </div>
    <div class="cl-relationships"><div class="cl-result-heading"><h3>Follow the product name</h3><span data-result-state>Before the merge</span></div>
      {targets.map((fixture, i) => <article class="cl-relation" data-triple={fixture.tripleId} data-target={i}>
        <header><span>{fixture.label}</span><span class="cl-type">Product</span></header>
        <div class="cl-edge"><span data-identity={i === 1 ? 'subject' : undefined} data-before={fixture.states.before.row.subject} data-merged={fixture.states.merged.row.subject} data-restored={fixture.states.restored.row.subject}>{fixture.states.before.row.subject}</span><span class="cl-predicate">{fixture.states.before.row.predicate.replaceAll('_', ' ')} <Icon name="arrow-right" /></span><span data-identity={i === 0 ? 'object' : undefined} data-before={fixture.states.before.row.object} data-merged={fixture.states.merged.row.object} data-restored={fixture.states.restored.row.object}>{fixture.states.before.row.object}</span></div>
        <p class="cl-field-change" data-field-status>Original {i === 0 ? 'object' : 'subject'} spelling</p>
        <details class="cl-source"><summary><span><Icon name="archive" /> Read source: {fixture.source.title}</span><Icon name="plus" /></summary><div><p class="cl-source-label">Fictional source conversation {fixture.source.conversationId}</p><blockquote>{fixture.source.content}</blockquote><p><Icon name="check" /> This relationship keeps the same source before merge, after merge and after inverse.</p><details class="cl-hash"><summary>Inspect the source and row hashes</summary><dl><dt>conversation_id in all three states</dt><dd>{fixture.source.conversationId}</dd><dt>Unchanged conversation SHA-256</dt><dd><code>{fixture.source.conversationFullRowHashes.before}</code></dd><dt>Unchanged message SHA-256</dt><dd><code>{fixture.source.messageFullRowHashes.before}</code></dd><dt>Triple row SHA-256 in the selected state</dt><dd><code data-row-hash data-before={fixture.states.before.fullRowSha256} data-merged={fixture.states.merged.fullRowSha256} data-restored={fixture.states.restored.fullRowSha256}>{fixture.states.before.fullRowSha256}</code></dd></dl><p>Edited triple rows also record new review metadata. Their full-row hashes change even when the identity spelling is restored.</p></details></div></details>
      </article>)}
      <details class="cl-controls" open><summary><span><Icon name="check" /> Two controls stayed unchanged</span><Icon name="plus" /></summary><div class="cl-control-grid">{controls.map((fixture, i) => <article data-control={fixture.role}><span class="cl-source-label">{i === 0 ? 'Different type: place' : 'Unrelated object: product'}</span><h4>{fixture.label}</h4><p class="cl-control-edge">{fixture.states.before.row.subject} <span>{fixture.states.before.row.predicate} <Icon name="arrow-right" /></span> {fixture.states.before.row.object}</p><p class="cl-control-proof"><Icon name="check" /> Full row identical in all three states</p><details class="cl-source"><summary>Read source and unchanged hash <Icon name="plus" /></summary><div><p class="cl-source-label">Fictional conversation {fixture.source.conversationId}: {fixture.source.title}</p><blockquote>{fixture.source.content}</blockquote><code>{fixture.states.before.fullRowSha256}</code><p>Same conversation_id and full row hash before merge, after merge and after inverse.</p></div></details></article>)}</div></details>
    </div>
  </div>
  <noscript><div class="cl-nojs"><h3>The completed result</h3><p>The product-scoped merge changed triple 1’s object and triple 2’s subject from slate pad to slate tablet. An immediate batch inverse restored both identity fields. All four source links, both control rows, and all source conversation/message rows survived.</p><p>The sources and both audit receipts below work without JavaScript. The replay buttons need JavaScript.</p></div></noscript>
  <section class="cl-audits" aria-labelledby="cl-audit-title" id="cl-audits"><div class="cl-audit-intro"><p class="eyebrow">The actual edit ledger</p><h3 id="cl-audit-title">Read either receipt.<br /><em>Keep both in view.</em></h3><p>Both reads came from the existing audit endpoint. Batch labels below stand for the synthetic IDs preserved in the downloadable receipt.</p></div><div class="cl-audit-grid">{audits.map((audit, i) => <details class="cl-audit" data-audit={i === 0 ? 'forward' : 'inverse'}><summary><span><Icon name={i === 0 ? 'arrow-right' : 'undo'} /> {i === 0 ? 'Read the forward audit' : 'Read the inverse audit'}</span><Icon name="plus" /></summary><div class="cl-audit-body"><p class="cl-audit-result">{i === 0 ? 'Merge batch · 2 fields normalized' : 'Inverse batch · 2 fields restored'}</p><p class="cl-source-label">Recorded run: source={audit.response.run?.source} · canonicalize=2</p>{audit.response.actions?.map(action => <article class="cl-audit-action"><h4>Triple {action.triple_id} · {Object.keys(action.changes)[0]}</h4><div><span><small>Snapshot before this edit</small><strong>{action[Object.keys(action.changes)[0] as 'subject' | 'object']}</strong></span><Icon name="arrow-right" /><span><small>New value recorded</small><strong>{Object.values(action.changes)[0]}</strong></span></div></article>)}<p>{i === 0 ? 'The actual response reports affected=2. Each audit action carries the pre-edit identity and a map containing just its changed field.' : 'The actual response reports reverted=2 and not_invertible=0. Its original action IDs plus triple IDs correlate this new batch with the forward edits.'}</p><details class="cl-audit-technical"><summary>Read request and correlation details</summary><code>{audit.method} {audit.uri.split('?')[0]}?batch_id={i === 0 ? '[merge batch]' : '[inverse batch]'}</code><p>HTTP {audit.responseStatus}. Full synthetic batch/action IDs and exact response bodies are preserved in the JSON receipt.</p>{i === 1 && <ul>{execution.inverseCorrelation.map(link => <li>Forward action {link.originalActionId} connects to inverse action {link.inverseActionId} on triple {link.tripleId}.</li>)}</ul>}</details></div></details>)}</div></section>
  <details class="cl-method"><summary>What the execution proves, and where it stops <Icon name="plus" /></summary><div><p><strong>Actual path:</strong> the Laravel HTTP test kernel authenticated a fictional owner and executed the tagged validation, routes, controllers, curation service and disposable MySQL writes. The ledger’s <code>source=mcp</code> value is a recorded field; no live MCP transport or gateway authorization was exercised.</p><p><strong>Manual exact-string selection:</strong> the request supplies <code>from=Slate Pad</code>, <code>to=Slate Tablet</code>, <code>entity_type=product</code> and a reason. Names normalize to lowercase. The triples were seeded, so this does not demonstrate automatic extraction or semantic discovery.</p><p><strong>Immediate inverse:</strong> there is no compare-and-swap check. Reverting an older batch could overwrite a later change to the same identity field. This test applies the inverse immediately, with no intervening identity edit.</p><p><strong>Identity restored, review metadata retained:</strong> the target rows’ <code>prune_batch</code>, <code>reviewed_at</code> and <code>updated_at</code> record the inverse. Full target rows do not return to their original bytes. Both controls and all source conversation/message rows remain byte-for-byte unchanged.</p><p><strong>Profile boundary:</strong> the graph’s source profile groups exact labels without separating types. The typed mutation was verified; type-separated profile identities are outside this proof.</p><p><strong>Verification:</strong> {execution.verification.featureTests} feature tests / {execution.verification.featureAssertions} assertions passed, with {execution.verification.independentMechanicalChecks.toLocaleString('en')} additional mechanical checks of source files, responses and row hashes. No source patch, model inference, queue worker or production connection was needed. The owned runtime was removed.</p><dl><dt>PanelForge source</dt><dd><code>{execution.source.revision}</code> · {execution.source.tag}</dd><dt>Application changes</dt><dd>None</dd></dl><a href="/media/curation/receipt.json" class="text-link">Download the curated execution receipt <Icon name="arrow-up-right" /></a></div></details>
</section>
<script>import { initCuration } from './controller';document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-curation-lab]').forEach(initCuration);</script>
